From: MUSTARDTIGERFPV <122312693+MUSTARDTIGERFPV@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: allow jumbo frames on Zynq-7000

zynq_config does not set MACB_CAPS_JUMBO, so macb_change_mtu() rejects
any MTU above 1500 with EINVAL. zynqmp_config sets it along with
.jumbo_max_len, and the Zynq-7000 GEM has the same JML register that
macb_init() programs; do the same here.

The link still comes up at 1500, this only permits a larger MTU. The
GEM TX packet buffer is 4 KB: on a PlutoSky R2 frames pass up to MTU
3900 and fail at 4000. iio_readdev over GbE at 950 MHz: 59.0 -> 75.8
MB/s (bbr+fq), 76.0 -> 92.4 MB/s (cubic+pfifo_fast).

Signed-off-by: MUSTARDTIGERFPV <122312693+MUSTARDTIGERFPV@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c	2026-09-05 12:30:43
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c	2026-09-05 12:30:43
@@ -4960,10 +4960,11 @@
 
 static const struct macb_config zynq_config = {
 	.caps = MACB_CAPS_GIGABIT_MODE_AVAILABLE | MACB_CAPS_NO_GIGABIT_HALF |
-		MACB_CAPS_NEEDS_RSTONUBR,
+		MACB_CAPS_NEEDS_RSTONUBR | MACB_CAPS_JUMBO,
 	.dma_burst_length = 16,
 	.clk_init = macb_clk_init,
 	.init = macb_init,
+	.jumbo_max_len = 10240,
 	.usrio = &macb_default_usrio,
 };
 
